<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red Tower (Alanya)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1226</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red Tower is an octagonal defensive tower by the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alanya">Alanya</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast, built in 1226 by order of the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayqubad-i">Kayqubad I</a>. About 33 metres high and built of red brick on a stone base, it guarded the shipyard and port that made Alanya the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>' winter residence and naval base. It now houses a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-tower-alanya.jpg" alt="Red Tower (Alanya)" width="320" height="488" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kallerna · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alanya_Red_Tower_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
